1. Introduction

This document describes the technical architecture and implementation plan for the Orbital Star Ring Smart City, whose cognition is realised through the nine‑layer QUENNE Stack. It extends the Technical Specification (QS-OSR-001) by detailing how the layers integrate, communicate, and operate as a cohesive distributed system. The architecture is designed for extreme reliability, real‑time determinism, and evolutionary adaptability in the space environment.

---

2. Architectural Principles

Principle Description
Strict Layering Each layer consumes services only from the layer immediately below and provides services only to the layer immediately above. Cross‑layer shortcuts are prohibited to maintain modular certifiability.
Separation of Concerns Ethical governance (Layer 9), domain control (Layer 8), cognitive fusion (Layer 7), resource management (Layer 6), real‑time actuation (Layer 5), physical optimisation (Layer 4), specialised solvers (Layer 3), OS foundation (Layer 2), and hardware abstraction (Layer 1) are logically and physically separated.
Fault‑Tolerant by Design All critical functions employ triple‑modular redundancy (TMR), diverse software implementations, and Byzantine fault‑tolerant consensus where required.
Data‑Centric Communication Asynchronous message passing over a real‑time capable publish/subscribe bus forms the backbone of inter‑layer and intra‑layer communication.
Self‑Description Every component publishes its capabilities, health, and resource usage via a common discovery protocol, enabling dynamic orchestration.
Transparency & Auditability All decisions that affect residents or system safety are logged immutably and are explainable via the Triad’s ethical audit interface.

