5.3 Redundancy and Failover

· Triad: Triple‑redundant, active‑standby‑monitor. Outputs voted at FPGA level.
· Reactor Controllers: Each reactor has three independent controller lanes; any two can sustain full control.
· Fusion Nodes: N+2 sparing; world model is computed by primary, secondary, and verifier.
· Photonic Cores: Distributed; loss of ≤10% of nodes degrades accuracy gracefully.
· Network: Dual counter‑rotating rings; automatic failover <5 ms.

All persistent state (world model snapshots, ethical logs, reactor configuration) is stored in a distributed consensus‑based key‑value store (etcd) replicated across 5 nodes, each in a different segment.

