6.3 Simulation Environment

A high‑fidelity digital twin of the entire Star Ring runs on ground and in orbit (on Triad’s strategic node). It includes:

· Physics Engine: Bullet Physics with custom orbital dynamics, thermal and structural FEM.
· Sensor Simulation: Realistic noise models for all 100,000+ virtual sensors.
· AI Behaviour Emulation: All QUENNE stack layers simulated with identical APIs.

This environment is used for training the Booster Scheduler, validating reactor control algorithms, and conducting “what‑if” analyses.

6.4 Incremental Deployment

The system is deployed in four phases, each adding layers and capabilities:

1. Phase A (Ground Testbed): Layers 1,2,5,7 (HAL, Linux, Photonic test chip, Fusion) in a vacuum chamber.
2. Phase B (ISS Star Ring Node): Full stack except Quantum Annealer (simulated) and limited Triad.
3. Phase C (Partial Ring): All layers deployed; Quantum Annealer installed; Triad gains ethical veto power.
4. Phase D (Full Operation): All systems active; Triad assumes full governance.

