9. Security Architecture

9.1 Trust Boundaries

Four distinct trust zones are defined:

1. Ring‑Internal Critical: Triad, QNI, Photonic AI. Communication within this zone uses authenticated encryption with hardware security modules (HSM).
2. Ring‑Internal General: Fusion, Engineering, Booster, Storage, Edge Nodes. Protected by network segmentation and MAC.
3. External Space‑to‑Space: Visiting vehicles, EVA suits. Mutual TLS with certificates issued by the Star Ring CA.
4. Earth Link: Quantum‑key‑encrypted lasercom. QKD keys are mixed with conventional AES‑256‑GCM.

9.2 Cryptographic Services

· Random Number Generation: Quantum‑based random number generators on each Triad node.
· Key Management: Centralised PKI with offline root CA (stored on Earth). All node certificates have short validity (7 days) and are automatically renewed via the Booster Scheduler.
· QKD Integration: The Photonic AI generates entangled photon pairs; the resulting keys are fed into the Linux kernel’s cryptodev interface for use by IPSec and TLS.

9.3 Access Control

· Human operators (residents, ground control) authenticate via smart cards or biometrics.
· Role‑Based Access Control (RBAC) is enforced at every API endpoint.
· Service‑to‑service authentication uses SPIFFE (Secure Production Identity Framework for Everyone) with mutual TLS.

