10. Monitoring and Observability

10.1 Health Monitoring

· Every node runs a health agent that reports CPU, memory, temperature, and uptime to a central Fleet Monitoring Service.
· Failure prediction uses LSTM models on telemetry to predict imminent hardware faults; the Booster Scheduler then migrates workloads and schedules maintenance.

10.2 Distributed Tracing

· All gRPC and DDS messages carry W3C trace context.
· Traces are collected by Jaeger and used to debug end‑to‑end latency issues (e.g., from debris detection to manoeuvre command).

10.3 Logging

· Structured JSON logs are shipped via Fluentd to an Elasticsearch cluster.
· Logs are automatically analysed for security incidents and system anomalies.

